  "P-CSE201-DEV/CCO.topics": {
   "uid": "P-CSE201-DEV/CCO.topics",
   "local_id": "CCO.topics",
   "label": "ContextField",
   "props": {
    "status": "given",
    "raw": "Treatment of this list: starting hypotheses — may add/drop/reorder with justification.\nA. Object-oriented foundations: classes and objects, encapsulation, modularity, object relationships (association, composition), interfaces\nB. Inheritance and polymorphism: inheritance hierarchies, abstract classes, polymorphism via interfaces and inheritance, method resolution, immutability\nC. Generic and reusable code: generics, comparing and cloning objects, the collections framework\nD. Robust programs: exception handling, assertions, defensive and secure programming, I/O streams and serialization\nE. Testing and tooling: unit testing, debugging, version control as part of everyday development\nF. Designing before coding: use cases, UML class/sequence/use-case diagrams, object-oriented design of a problem\nG. Event-driven programming and GUIs\nH. Concurrency: threads, thread pools, mutual exclusion, race conditions and deadlocks, producer-consumer, speedup\nI. Design patterns: common creational, structural and behavioural patterns applied to real problems\n",
    "value": null
   },
   "version": 1,
   "status": "draft",
   "created_by": "G1",
   "prompt_id": "G1",
   "prompt_version": null,
   "model": null,
   "sources": [
    {
     "tag": "USER",
     "ref": "CCO.topics"
    }
   ],
   "ts": 1790770974.8126185
  },
  "P-CSE201-DEV/CCO.intent": {
   "uid": "P-CSE201-DEV/CCO.intent",
   "local_id": "CCO.intent",
   "label": "ContextField",
   "props": {
    "status": "given",
    "raw": "Central question the course answers: How do you design, build and test a multi-component program so that its parts can be developed independently and reused?\nPedagogical emphasis: design thinking before coding; writing code others can read, reuse and test; learning by building a substantial team project.\nThis course should NOT become:\n- a Java language features course\n- a data-structures course (that is covered by the prerequisite)\n- a lecture-only course without regular hands-on practice\n",
    "value": null
   },
   "version": 1,
   "status": "draft",
   "created_by": "G1",
   "prompt_id": "G1",
   "prompt_version": null,
   "model": null,
   "sources": [
    {
     "tag": "USER",
     "ref": "CCO.intent"
    }
   ],
   "ts": 1790770974.812624
  },
